  "brief": "This article introduces the 'Alien Zoo', an experimental framework designed to study the usability of counterfactual explanations (CFEs) for machine learning models. CFEs are a type of post-hoc explanation that show users what input changes would alter the model's prediction. The framework, presented as a web-based game, targets novice users in a low-knowledge domain to evaluate how CFEs help them understand and learn from an automated system. A proof-of-concept user study demonstrated that users receiving CFEs performed better on learning tasks and reported higher subjective usability compared to those with no explanations. The work aims to provide a tool for human-grounded evaluation of explainable AI (XAI) to complement technology-oriented research, with all code and data provided for reproducibility."
